AB  - Accurate identification of crop growth stages plays a vital role in agricultural decision-making and resource management. However, subtle morphological variations and the high visual similarity between adjacent growth stages pose significant challenges for reliable recognition. To address this issue, this study proposes an efficient classification method based on an improved You Only Look Once Version 8 (YOLOv8n-cls) model. Firstly, an effective downsampling (EDown) module is designed with a dual-branch architecture to minimize information loss during the downsampling process. Additionally, a cross-stage partial bottleneck with omni-dimensional dynamic convolution (C2f-ODConv) module is introduced to enable dynamic feature extraction, thereby enhancing the model’s capacity to capture structural differences across various growth stages. Finally, a triplet attention (TA) mechanism is incorporated, combining channel attention and spatial-directional dependencies to improve the model’s focus on key regions while effectively suppressing background interference. In the classification task involving ten growth stages of winter wheat, the proposed method achieved an accuracy of 96.11%, outperforming 13 mainstream image classification models. This study provides a solid theoretical foundation and practical reference for the accurate classification of winter wheat growth stages under field conditions.
