AB  - The problem of trajectory filtering has garnered significant attention across various domains. However, existing methods struggle with complex situations and perform poorly under model mismatch conditions. To address these limitations, this paper proposes KalmanTNet, a novel data-model hybrid driven approach that leverages the robust sequence processing capabilities of the Transformer architecture and the concise structure of the Kalman filter. Experimental results show that KalmanTNet outperforms Kalman filter, extended Kalman filter, unscented Kalman filter and KalmanNet in complex environments, achieving superior filtering accuracy.
